pītaka,
(1) adj. and subst., ifc. one that has drunk, in viṣa-pītaka (= Skt. ˚pīta), one that has drunk poison (specifying -ka ?): Mmk 〔462.26〕; subst. (= Skt. pīta), drink: Av 〔i.179.6 f.〕;
(2) n. of two nāga kings (? from the other Skt. pīta, yellow): Māy 〔247.14〕 dvau Pītakau nāgarājānau.
